<title>USA: Kimberly-Clark says sold mill to alliance.</title>
<headline>Kimberly-Clark says sold mill to alliance.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kimberly-Clark Corp said Thursday that it has sold its pulp and newsprint mill, inventories and related woodlands at Coosa Pines, Ala. for $602.7 million in cash.</p>
<p>The buyer, said the company, was Alliance Forest Products, a Montreal-based company.</p>
<p>Kimberly-Clark said that the sale of the mill will allow it to focus attention on its core businesses of personal care, consumer tissue and away-from-home products.</p>
</text>
